# ============================================================
# Dr Manoj Clinic Automation — .gitignore
# CODE ONLY repo. Secrets and patient data must NEVER be committed.
# When in doubt, this file errs on the side of blocking.
# ============================================================

# ---- SECRETS: environment files ----
.env
.env.*
*.env
# (allow the safe templates only)
!*.env.example
!.env.example

# ---- SECRETS: keys / credentials (service-account JSON, tokens, certs) ----
# Block ALL .json by default so a key file can never slip in.
*.json
# allow only clearly-safe example/template json
!*.example.json
!dashboard/appsscript.json

# S203: signatures.json is the Marg REPORT SIGNATURE REGISTRY -- report types,
# title patterns and the end_marker that proves an export is complete. It holds
# no secrets (checked), and it is one of the files that existed ONLY on the two
# Windows PCs until S203. The blanket *.json rule above exists to keep
# credentials out; it was also silently excluding this. PUBLISH_ALL refused the
# whole push rather than drop it -- F-100's guard working exactly as intended.
!**/signatures.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*-key.*
*credentials*
*secret*
*token*

# ---- CONTACT NUMBERS: F-185. Never in this repository, in any format. ----
# The PATIENT-DATA block below blocks .csv/.tsv/.xls/.xlsx and says nothing
# about .json. On 28-Aug a kit shipped 18 real supplier numbers in a .json
# inside deploy_kits and nothing would have stopped the next publish. Numbers
# live in the config store beside the archive, never here.
*phone*.json
*phones*
*contact*.json
*contacts*
*mobile*.json
_config/

# ---- PATIENT DATA: exports, mirrors, logs, recordings ----
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.jsonl
*.mp3
*.wav
*.vcf
wa_logs/
recordings/
exports/
uploads/
data/
data_backup_09_jun/
outputs/
Archive/


# ---- PYTHON runtime / build junk ----
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---- OS / editor noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# ---- Logs ----
*.log
recordings-archive/client_secret.json
recordings-archive/drive_token.json
recordings-archive/__pycache__/
!recordings-archive/get_drive_token.py

# ---- ATTENDANCE subsystem secrets (Session 59) ----
# att_config.py holds the attendance dashboard password + SECRET_KEY — NEVER commit.
# The non-secret attendance code (att_dashboard.py, att_core.py, attlistener_v2.py) IS committable.
att_config.py
attendance/att_config.py
console.db
console.db.tmp
transcript_cache.db
console_reviews.db
rec_cache/
*.tmp
attendance/staff_master.csv
# ---- Clinic Finance (S179) · PHI + money. MUST be in .gitignore BEFORE the
# ---- first commit of finance_app.py, not after (F-31 / F-49).
finance/finance.db
finance/finance.db-wal
finance/finance.db-shm
finance/finance.db.bak*
finance/scans/
finance/exports/
finance/access.log
finance/medical_legacy.csv
finance/medical_*.csv
finance/finance.db
finance/finance.db-wal
finance/finance.db-shm
finance/finance.db.bak*
finance/finance.db.pre*
finance/scans/
finance/exports/
finance/vendor/
finance/access.log
finance/backup.log
finance/medical_legacy.csv
finance/medical_*.csv
finance/upi_statements/
finance/marg_in/
finance/*_bills.csv
finance/*_items.csv
finance/REPORT_1.XLS
finance/REPORT_1.xls




# scratch: files staged for deletion via device bridge (device_bash cannot rm)
/_to_delete/

# S218: the staff-cards registry is names+URLs only (no PHI, no secrets) and must publish
!deploy_kits/*/cards_registry.json
